<article-title>Time-resolved optical mammography between 637 and 985&#x000a0;nm: clinical study on the detection and identification of breast lesions</article-title><source>Phys Med Biol</source><year>2005</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>2469</fpage><lpage>2488</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1088/0031-9155/50/11/003</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Taroni P, Torricelli A, Spinelli L et al (2005) Time-resolved optical mammography between 637 and 985&#x000a0;nm: clinical study on the detection and identification of breast lesions. Phys Med Biol 50:2469&#x02013;2488 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15901949</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tromberg</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cerussi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Shah</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Imaging in breast cancer: diffuse optics in breast cancer: detecting tumors in pre-menopausal women and monitoring neoadjuvant chemotherapy</article-title><source>Breast Cancer Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>279</fpage><lpage>285</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/bcr1358</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Tromberg BJ, Cerussi A, Shah N et al (2005) Imaging in breast cancer: diffuse optics in breast cancer: detecting tumors in pre-menopausal women and monitoring neoadjuvant chemotherapy. Breast Cancer Res 7:279&#x02013;285 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16457705</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Cronin</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name><name><surname>Currier</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Benign versus malignant breast masses: optical differentiation with US-guided optical imaging reconstruction</article-title><source>Radiology</source><year>2005</year><volume>237</volume><fpage>57</fpage><lpage>66</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1148/radiol.2371041236</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Zhu Q, Cronin EB, Currier AA et al (2005) Benign versus malignant breast masses: optical differentiation with US-guided optical imaging reconstruction. Radiology 237:57&#x02013;66 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16183924</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chance</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Nioka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Breast cancer detection based on incremental biochemical and physiological properties of breast cancers: a six-year, two-site study</article-title><source>Acad Radiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>925</fpage><lpage>933</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.acra.2005.04.016</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Chance B, Nioka S, Zhang J et al (2005) Breast cancer detection based on incremental biochemical and physiological properties of breast cancers: a six-year, two-site study. Acad Radiol 12:925&#x02013;933 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16023383</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR19"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Floery</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Helbich</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Riedl</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Characterization of benign and malignant breast lesions with computed tomography laser mammograp